  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#48858\", \"PowerToys#47430\"], \"answer\": \"This is a known issue: the Command Palette Dock does not persist the network adapter chosen via 'Next Network' (or in the network flyout), so after a restart or reboot it falls back to the wrong adapter (e.g. the unused Ethernet NIC) and shows zeros. The past tickets don't describe a permanent fix. Workarounds reported: disable the unused wired adapter/connection so the dock defaults to the Wi-Fi one, or after each reboot re-select the correct network in the flyout (toggling the Dock off/on in CmdPal settings can help refresh the values, though the selection itself doesn't persist across disabling/enabling CmdPal). Add your report and the bug report ZIP to PowerToys#48858 so the maintainers can track it.\"}",
